    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0661" n="585" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg585"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5631/205a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Emmet</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-15T18:00:00-04:00">May 15, 1935—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. We exchanged desiderata<anchor n="9" xml:id="d474-f1"/> this morning with van
                    Breugel. We handed to him at the same time a set of the general
                        provisions<anchor n="9" xml:id="d474-f2"/> which we propose for inclusion in
                    the trade agreement. Similar copies were handed to van Breugel some weeks ago.
                    He seems to consider that they were handed to him in a sort of personal way but
                    he said that he had nevertheless sent copies to his Government. Van Breugel was
                    told that we would be glad to go forward with negotiations with regard to the
                    general provisions immediately if his Government was so inclined. He had said
                    that he could not indicate when negotiations in other respects might be started
                    until after his Government had received our list.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
